Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:43:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(notify): release removed-board observers during existing
 handle sweep [daveey]

Problem: independent review of PR4014 reproduced three deleted SQLite fds
remaining after board_signature, directory removal and gone-board sweep.
Why 1: the notification-only retained observer outlives its last read.
Why 2: gone-board housekeeping enumerated old reader domains, not this new one.
Root (happened): introducing a retained read domain omitted its integration
with the existing idle-only removed-board retention contract.
Root (not caught): replacement/reset/cap tests exercise paths read again;
none composed board_signature with removing a board that is never read again.
Recurrence: prior generic-reader gone-board cleanup already handles this
lifecycle; PR4014 moved retention outside that registry without its sweep hook.

Use existing path_gone semantics, snapshot and recheck exact registry custody,
nonblocking borrower and lifecycle acquisition, and preserve busy entries for
later sweeps. Keep live boards, avoid double-counting empty/evicted readers.
Sweep only modules already imported; no generic reader behavior changes.

Proof: real-fd regression RED on reviewed27f2e34376 (three behavioral failures
plus absent-method check), GREEN after. Seven boundary mutants killed with
real SQL/descriptor tests, including borrowed nonblocking behavior, lifecycle
custody, live/reappeared paths, registry replacement and empty counts.
187 consumer files,3274 tests pass without file retries. Full scripts/check:
21 checks green. Original scan amplification benchmark remains a controlled
reproduction, not sole historical timeout causation or incident recovery.
Natural deployment only; final activation/30-minute detector window remain
with incident owner t_e39e99d8b9d544dd.
